  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A bar magnet is passing through a conducting loop of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The radius of the bar magnet is such that it just passes through the loop. The induced e.m.f. in the loop can be represented by the approximate curve:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0077_3466d6181a01.png\" style=\"width: 102px; height: 161px;\" />&nbsp;<img src=\"assets\\qt0077_578c65644fbe.png\" style=\"width: 290px; height: 194px;\" /></p>"
  },
